"Where is AI?"
AI is everywhere people are using it to find answers to questions and in my future work I hope to be doing which is R&D scientist some are even using it to compile and analyze data that they collect

Students identify AI systems they interact with every day and classify:

What the AI does

The AI analyzes the datasets and comes up with answers or can give you the general answer to a question based on the current knowledge of the field, mine is biology

What data it uses

Usually for biology the AI would use numerical data, figures, or graphs from experiment reports or papers to help answer questions and draw conclusions. It could also use data from advanced programs that model protein folding or chemical reactions.

What business problem it solves

This could solve the problem of having to go through thousands of data points to try and graph/model the data to find how the data relates, you could ask AI and it could potentially find the relationship faster than normal methods.

Who benefits

The laboratory conducting experiments could potentially benefit because they would become more efficient and maybe be able to streamline the experiment processes with the use of AI helping to speed up certain parts. Scientists/Students would also benefit because it could make their work easier.

What could go wrong

Like with all AI use it could potentially hallucinate and just make up relationships between data, or maybe even fabricate data that was not collected to help it make up a relationship between the data. 
